Make = without an address print the number of the last line.
POSIX gives = the default address $, so a bare = prints the number of
lines in the buffer, as in other implementations of ed. This ed used the
current line instead, so "=" printed the current line number and scripts
written for other eds got the wrong count. Use $ when no address is
given.

---
 editors/ed.c |    3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/editors/ed.c
+++ b/editors/ed.c
@@ -1014,7 +1014,8 @@
 			break;
 
 		case '=':
-			printf("%d\n", num1);
+			/* The default address is "$" */
+			printf("%d\n", have1 ? num1 : lastNum);
 			break;
 		case '\0':
 			if (have1) {
